# The caps (report 037 section 2.4): a 100 KB note opens in the preview (at most 400 blocks, then the muted "Preview
# truncated" line) and in the editor (under the 128 KB cap), and what is typed at its end is saved; a 200 KB note opens
# read-only in the preview (Edit says why); a file that is not UTF-8 opens read-only too, its bytes never rewritten.
seed big "Big 100.md" 100
seed big "Big 200.md" 200
seed text "Latin1.md" "# Caf\xe9\n\nNot UTF-8.\n"
wait 900
key ctrl-p
type big 100
key enter
wait 1500
expect state page preview
expect state truncated 1
expect state blocks 400
key end
wait 400
expect text "^Preview truncated"
shot 01-truncated
key ctrl-e
wait 1500
expect state page editor
key ctrl-end
type The end.
wait 1900
expect state last_save ok
expect file "Big 100.md" contains "a plain item\n\nThe end."
shot 02-big-editor
key esc
wait 600
key ctrl-p
type big 200
key enter
wait 1500
expect state page preview
expect state caption "Preview  ·  read only, over 128 KB  ·  Ctrl+O: options"
shot 03-read-only
key ctrl-e
wait 300
expect state page preview
expect state notice "Read only: notes over 128 KB are not edited here"
key esc
wait 400
key ctrl-p
type latin1
key enter
# (the notice of Edit stays 4 s in the grey line)
wait 4000
expect state page preview
expect state caption "Preview  ·  read only, not UTF-8  ·  Ctrl+O: options"
shot 04-not-utf8
key ctrl-e
wait 300
expect state page preview
expect file "Latin1.md" contains "Caf\xe9"
